WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.940
Many people think of science as
apolitical--concerned with facts, not

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.070
political views values or opinions. However, when it comes to science-based

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:20.520
policy and legislation, science no longer
seems unbiased. The prevalence of

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.020
opinions and biases in policy debates
has led countless members of the

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.910
scientific community to avoid policy
debates despite their ability to provide

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:34.739
helpful contributions. 
However, science and politics are more

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:40.380
intertwined than most people realize. 
Science helps lawmakers write policies

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:46.260
and regulations that affect our everyday
lives. At the same time, government shape

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.060
science through budgets, laws and
regulations. Using NASA, the National

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:56.790
Aeronautics and Space Administration, as
an example, let's walk through how our

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:02.790
federal policies have shaped research. In
2018, Congress provided NASA with an

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:08.340
annual operating budget of 16.5 billion dollars. Why did the federal

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.200
government invest so heavily in NASA's
research? First, public demand for

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.110
scientific research can strongly
influence politicians. Motivated by

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:24.060
increasing public concern, lawmakers have
funded research to investigate climate

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:30.000
change's causes and mitigate its effects. This research is closely tied to NASA's

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.369
work in outer space: satellites monitor
Earth's atmosphere, and solar panels,

00:01:35.369 --> 00:01:40.369
which power most spacecraft, are an
emerging alternative to fossil fuels.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:46.350
Congress also funds research because it
recognizes the potential for research to

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.360
have broad societal impacts in
unexpected ways. As a result, many

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.060
groundbreaking technologies, like GPS and
advanced prosthetic limbs, have their

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:03.630
roots in NASA technology. Second, global
competition and national security

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:09.450
concerns motivate federal funding for
NASA. The Space Race, which was one of the

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:14.310
many arenas in which the United States
and the Soviet Union fought the Cold War,

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.870
ushered in NASA's growth. 
After the Soviet Union shocked the

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:24.360
United States by building Sputnik, the
world's first orbiting spacecraft, NASA's

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.879
successful moon landing in 1969 restored
national pride and garnered

00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:35.430
international recognition. NASA has also
developed numerous military aviation

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:41.190
technologies, like composite materials,
fly-by-wire cockpits and wingtip

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.690
winglets, that were later adapted for
commercial aircraft. Government

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:51.420
priorities shift with time, and this is
reflected in NASA's budget.For example,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:56.129
near the height of the Space Race in
1966, the fraction of the federal budget

00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:01.980
dedicated to NASA was almost 10 times
as large as it is today. By contrast,

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.940
adjusted for today's dollars, the
National Institute of Health's budget

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:12.870
grew threefold between 1970 in 2005. Now,
let's examine how science influences

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:18.690
policy. Many beneficial laws, like the
Clean Air Act of 1970, have been the

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:23.010
result of scientific research, and
scientists are frequently consulted as

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.780
experts when bills are drafted.
Scientific research also serves as the

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:32.639
basis for entire federal institutions
like the Department of Energy, which

00:03:32.639 --> 00:03:38.840
regulates nuclear material and funds
energy-related research. As we can see,

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:44.910
scientific research shapes policy and
vice-versa. Every generation has new

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.260
challenges that need scientific
solutions. Ensuring that our nation's

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:54.389
students are provided the education and
training to meet these challenges, both

00:03:54.389 --> 00:04:01.549
through science and policy, is crucial to
the success of our nation and the world

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.160
you

